ntdll: Bridge Apple's GPTK 4 D3DMetal onto wine 11.14.

Ported from rishiad/soju-wine, which proves the approach on wine 11.0.  Upstream
MR !6866 switched macOS from TSD coexistence to gsbase swapping and names
D3DMetal as a casualty that "will need to be changed to use Unix calls"; this is
that route rather than a port of CrossOver's TSD model.

Three mechanisms:
  - ntdll loads libd3dshared.dylib, flips its internal enableUnixCall flag by
    walking the mach-o symtab, and calls its three Patch* entry points, so the
    PE side reaches wine through __wine_unix_call instead of jumping straight
    into native code
  - every native PE region is registered with rosetta via
    register_non_native_code_region, which is what lets rosetta use the windows
    TEB for %gs inside those regions -- the TLS seam is crossed on Apple's side
    rather than by changing wine's
  - D3DMetal's own worker threads are detected by their thunk prologue and
    routed through __wine_native_thread_start, so they run with a native stack

Ported rather than applied: soju's patches are zero-context diffs against wine
11.0 and place purely by line number, so most hunks land in the wrong function
on 11.14.  Each was re-placed against a named anchor, plus three real changes:

  - struct ntdll_thread_data and ntdll_get_thread_data() were renamed to
    struct thread_data and get_thread_data() in wine 11
  - NtCreateThreadEx no longer assigns thread_data->start itself; wine 11 moved
    that into create_server_thread(), so the thread bridge hooks there instead,
    which also covers PsCreateSystemThread since it shares the helper
  - virtual_map_module() was restructured; the native-region registration now
    hangs off the STATUS_IMAGE_ALREADY_LOADED path, which is the case where a
    real PE image was mapped rather than replaced by a builtin

Builds clean; ntdll.so exports __wine_native_thread_start, run_native_thread,
register_non_native_code_region and winemac.so exports macdrv_functions.
Runtime behaviour is not yet verified.
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/ntdll.spec b/dlls/ntdll/ntdll.spec
index d0912cc..5db62c3 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/ntdll.spec
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/ntdll.spec
@@ -208,6 +208,7 @@
 @ stdcall -syscall NtCreateSymbolicLinkObject(ptr long ptr ptr)
 @ stdcall -syscall=0x004e NtCreateThread(ptr long ptr long ptr ptr ptr long)
 @ stdcall -syscall NtCreateThreadEx(ptr long ptr long ptr ptr long long long long ptr)
+@ stdcall -private __wine_native_thread_start(ptr)
 @ stdcall -syscall NtCreateTimer(ptr long ptr long)
 @ stdcall -syscall NtCreateToken(ptr long ptr long ptr ptr ptr ptr ptr ptr ptr ptr ptr)
 @ stdcall -syscall NtCreateTransaction(ptr long ptr ptr long long long long ptr ptr)
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/thread.c b/dlls/ntdll/thread.c
index fe083be..a8ee93c 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/thread.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/thread.c
@@ -229,6 +229,19 @@ void set_native_thread_name( DWORD tid, const char *name )
         NtClose(h);
 }
 
+/***********************************************************************
+ *           __wine_native_thread_start  (NTDLL.@)
+ */
+ULONG WINAPI __wine_native_thread_start( void *arg )
+{
+    struct native_thread_params params = { 0 };
+    NTSTATUS status;
+
+    (void)arg;
+    if ((status = WINE_UNIX_CALL( unix_run_native_thread, &params ))) return status;
+    return params.result;
+}
+
 
 /***********************************************************************
  *           RtlExitUserThread  (NTDLL.@)
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
index e9b8375..4a6853b 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loader.c
@@ -67,6 +67,8 @@
